---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
const lang = 'en';
---
<Layout
  title="Every raid, I've scouted it myself · CDM Motorsport"
  description="Scouting the motorcycle rally-raid routes in Morocco: every itinerary is checked on the ground, in advance, for a dirt bike tour that truly means something."
  ogImage="/img/reco-raids-hero.jpg"
  lang={lang}
>
  <section class="phero short" style="background-image:url('/img/reco-raids-hero.jpg')">
    <div class="wrap c">
      <div class="eyebrow" style="color:#e8c9a6">Behind the scenes</div>
      <h1>Raid <em>scouting</em></h1>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="pad">
    <div class="wrap article">
      <div class="meta reveal">Behind the scenes · 4 min read</div>
      <div class="big reveal" style="margin-bottom:24px">
        Every raid, I've <em>scouted it</em><br />myself
      </div>
      <div class="reveal">
        <p>
          There's one thing I never compromise on: not a single one of our 7 raids has been
          drawn on a map from behind a desk. Each one, I've scouted myself, on the ground,
          before taking you there. To me, that's the foundation of a real raid, and it's
          what makes the difference.
        </p>
        <p>
          I've known Morocco for close to 25 years. This country, its pistes and its
          people, I've learned them over the years, and that changes everything when it
          comes to laying out a route. I know where the sand gets tricky, where a track
          fades after the rains, where to find fuel at the right moment, and most of all
          where the most beautiful passages hide, the ones you won't find on any map.
        </p>

        <figure class="reco-video reveal">
          <video
            controls
            preload="metadata"
            playsinline
            poster="/videos/reco-raids-poster.jpg"
          >
            <source src="/videos/reco-raids.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
          </video>
          <figcaption>
            A glimpse of a scouting run, at the wheel of the 4x4 along the Atlantic.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>

        <p>
          Scouting a raid means going back out there, often by 4x4 and motorcycle, and
          riding every stage in advance. I check the state of the pistes, the real
          difficulty of each section, the water and fuel points, the hotels where we'll
          sleep, and safety from end to end. Nothing is left to chance, because it's that
          invisible work that lets you, once you're on site, think about nothing but
          riding and enjoying yourself.
        </p>
        <p>
          It's also what lets me adapt each route to the conditions of the moment, and
          offer you itineraries that have meaning, rhythm and beauty. When you follow the
          track, you're following a path I've already ridden, tested and chosen for you.
        </p>
        <p>
          At heart, that's the CDM Motorsport spirit: raids designed by someone who
          actually rides, not off-the-shelf circuits bought from a catalog.
        </p>

        <p style="margin-top:28px">
          Want to ride terrain that's been scouted meter by meter?
        </p>
        <a href="/en/#raids" class="btn dark" style="margin-top:14px">Discover the raids</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .reco-video {
    margin: 32px auto;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 14px;
  }
  .reco-video video {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 360px;
    max-height: 72vh;
    aspect-ratio: 9 / 16;
    background: #141008;
    border-radius: 4px;
    display: block;
    object-fit: cover;
  }
  .reco-video figcaption {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 13px;
    color: #7a7064;
    text-align: center;
    max-width: 480px;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  @media (max-width: 540px) {
    .reco-video video {
      max-width: 100%;
      max-height: 80vh;
    }
  }
</style>
